  "raw": {
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/193453": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Digital Marketing-Tenure Track",
      "description": "Department: Simpson College Location: Simpson College The Multimedia Communication and Graphic Design Department at Simpson College is seeking applications for a full-time, tenure-track, assistant professor in Marketing Communication for the 2027-2028 academic year. We seek a dynamic candidate committed to teaching who has expertise in digital and social media strategy, brand management, and marketing communication. Ideal candidates will demonstrate an understanding of audience engagement, content analytics, and visual storytelling across multiple platforms. Experience in sports communication or working with athletic brands and teams is highly desirable. Responsibilities ·         Teach six courses (or a 3-3 load) including core undergraduate courses such as Intro to Communication, Media & PR Writing and Public Relations. Other courses would depend on expertise but could include courses in digital communication, social media management, integrated marketing communication, brand strategy and ethical use of artificial intelligence. ·         Contribute to the Simpson community and the department by advising students, teaching first-year courses, engaging in professional development and being involved in service to the broader campus community. ·         Supervise experiential learning opportunities such as interdisciplinary student-run projects, internships and undergraduate research. ·         Ph.D. in Communication, Media Studies, or a related field preferred; master’s degree with significant professional experience in digital marketing, brand management, or sports communication will be strongly considered. ·         Demonstrated expertise with digital and social media strategy, audience analytics, and storytelling. ·         Evidence of effective teaching or mentoring in higher education or in a professional setting. Applicants should submit a cover letter, a current vitae (including names of three references), and graduate transcripts (unofficial). The cover letter should highlight professional accomplishments and relevant teaching experience.  Teaching evaluations, a teaching philosophy statement and other evidence of excellent mentoring may be submitted as well. Applicants must be authorized to work for any employer in the U.S. We are unable to sponsor or take over sponsorship of an employment visa at this time. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the job is filled. Applications received by Dec. 1, 2026 will receive priority consideration."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/192603": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Sport Administration-Tenure Track",
      "description": "Department: Simpson College Location: Simpson College ·         Teach six courses per year, consistent with departmental need and candidate’s training and interests. Courses may include sport sales, sport finance, sport facility and event management, sport marketing, and sport business courses applicable within the general education curriculum. ·         Contribute to student success and recruitment, engage in the general education program, advise students and student clubs, and incorporate experiential learning into coursework. ·         Help the department explore graduate opportunities in the field. ·         Terminal degree in sport management or a related field is required. PhD or EdD preferred (ABD considered). ·         Evidence of successful, innovative college-level teaching experience with the ability to utilize classroom technology. ·         Demonstrate on-going commitment to each individual student’s needs for success. ·         Demonstrate the ability to develop partnerships and collaborate with colleagues to facilitate student experiential learning, research, and internship opportunities. ·         Willingness to participate in department activities, service to the college, and ability to work with faculty, staff, and students in a collegial and cooperative manner. Interested candidates should submit the following materials: Cover letter specifying the instrument(s) you are applying to teach and outlining your qualifications. Current resume or curriculum vitae Unofficial transcripts (official transcripts required upon hire). Contact information for three professional references. Applicants must be authorized to work for any employer in the U.S. We are unable to sponsor or take over sponsorship of an employment visa at this time. Application Deadline: Applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis until the positions are filled."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/123054": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor - Business, Accounting & Economics",
      "description": "Department: Simpson College: Academic Affairs: Simpson Online Location: Indianola, IA The Business, Accounting and Economics Department at Simpson College is accepting application to build an Adjunct teaching pool. Courses may be offer in person and throught the Simpson Online program. We seek candidates who will be knowledgeable and committed to providing a rigorous learning experience for students. A master’s degree is required. Preferred Qualifications: Experience teaching both online and in person. Applicants should submit a cover letter; please highlight interest in and qualifications for this position, as well as any relevant teaching experience, a current vitae, names and contact information of three professional references, graduate transcripts (unofficial). Applicants must be authorized to work for any employer in the U.S. We are unable to sponsor or take over sponsorship of an employment visa at this time. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/189342": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty – Applied Music (Voice)",
      "description": "Department: Simpson College Location: Indianola, IA Position Summary: Simpson College is seeking qualified and passionate educators for part-time Adjunct Faculty positions in Applied Music. We are currently hiring specialists in voice to provide individualized and/or group instruction to music majors and non-majors. These positions are ideal for professional musicians and educators who are committed to student success and artistic excellence. Key Responsibilities: Provide applied instruction in voice for majors and non-majors Prepare and deliver course materials, including syllabi Evaluate student progress through performances, assignments, and assessments. Offer constructive feedback and mentorship to students. Participate in departmental juries and recitals. Maintain professional standards in teaching and musicianship. Minimum Qualifications: Master’s degree in Music or a closely related field from an accredited institution. Demonstrated expertise in vocal performance Strong communication and interpersonal skills . Ability to work effectively with a diverse student population. Preferred Qualifications: College-level teaching experience. Active performance career or professional experience in art song and opera, with familiarity with musical theatre . Familiarity with digital tools for music instruction Interested candidates should submit the following materials: Cover letter specifying the instrument(s) you are applying to teach and outlining your qualifications. Current resume or curriculum vitae Unofficial transcripts (official transcripts required upon hire). Contact information for three professional references. Application Deadline: Applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis until the positions are filled."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/191426": {
      "title": "Director of Human Resources",
      "description": "Department: Simpson College Location: Indianola Simpson College Simpson College is a four-year private college of the liberal arts and sciences affiliated with the United Methodist Church. Located just 12 miles south of Des Moines, the capital of Iowa, Simpson’s picturesque 75-acre campus in Indianola is home to more than 1,200 full-time undergraduate students with an additional 100 students enrolled in online and graduate programs, and hundreds of faculty and staff members. The College has a strong academic reputation and is a highly relational student-centric institution, placing significant value on high-impact and co-curricular learning. Simpson is Iowa's top-ranked private college and #5 overall in the recently released 2026 U.S. News & World Report Regional Midwest rankings. Simpson is also #1 in Iowa for \"Best Value\" while also earning a #4 overall ranking for the Midwest. The City of Indianola is home to Simpson and is a flourishing, collaborative, and growing community of 16,000 people. It has a charming, central town square with thriving restaurants and coffee shops. Greater Des Moines serves as the government, commercial, cultural, and recreational hub for the state of Iowa. Des Moines prides itself on its vibrant economy, world-class amenities, friendly communities, short commutes, affordable housing, excellent education system, and high-quality health care. Position Summary Provides strategic leadership and oversight of all human resources functions, ensuring alignment with organizational goals, legal requirements, and best practices. Serves as a trusted advisor to executive leadership and management, supporting employee relations, workforce planning, and organizational effectiveness. Leads efficient, equitable , and compliant HR operations by leveraging data, technology, and continuous improvement to support a high-performing workplace culture. Serves as the organization’s Title IX Coordinator, overseeing compliance, investigations, training, and response processes to ensure adherence to federal and institutional Title IX requirements. Essen tial Job Functions Provide strategic leadership for the human resources function by developing and administering HR policies, programs, and practices that align with the college’s mission, values, and strategic priorities, including direct supervision of Payroll and Benefits staff. Estimated time: 2 5 % Ensure compliance and manage institutional risk by overseeing adherence to federal and state employment laws and higher-education regulations, including Title IX, ADA, FLSA, FMLA, and related reporting and training requirements, with functional oversight of payroll- and benefits-related compliance activities. Estimated time: 20% Lead employee relations and performance management efforts by advising leadership, addressing workplace concerns, supporting performance evaluation processes, and ensuring consistent application of policies. Estimated time: 15% Oversee recruitment, hiring, onboarding, and retention for faculty and staff to support workforce planning, diversity, and institutional effectiveness, coordinating with search committees and administrative partners as needed. Estimated time: 15% Serve as the Title IX Coordinator by overseeing Title IX policies, training, investigations, case management, and response processes to ensure equitable , timely , and compliant resolution of matters. Estimated time: 15% Administer compensation, benefits, and position classification programs by ensuring equitable pay practices, competitive benefits offerings, and alignment with budgetary and regulatory requirements, including direct supervision of benefits administration and payroll operations. Estimated time: 5% Develop and deliver training and professional development initiatives for faculty, staff, and supervisors related to compliance, leadership, and workplace expectations. Estimated time: 5% A bachelor's degree in human resources management, business administration, or a related field, or an equivalent combination of education and experience. 3 - 5 years’ human resources experience working as HR Business Partner or Director of Human Resources. Professional certification in Human Resources (PHR) and/or SHRM-CP desired . Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Ideal start date is 10/01/2026. A complete application will include: Cover letter addressing your interest in the position Resume Contact information of three professional references"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/190965": {
      "title": "Assistant Coach - Men's Gymnastics",
      "description": "Department: Simpson College: Athletics: Gymnastics Location: Indianola Assist Head Coach in management of the men’s gymnastics team. Duties include but are not limited to coaching, recruiting, and travel logistics. Essential job functions include: Assist in the direction of workouts. (40%) - Create and execute training plans for 3 events; Improvise in the gym; Advise and manage routine construction. Coach at Competitions (20%) - Set lineups; Equipment setup for home competitions; Travel to all away competitions; Know routines and be prepared for inquiries. Recruit prospective student athletes. (20%) - Assess skill level and competitiveness of high school athletes; Communicate clearly and professionally with prospective athletes; Participate in on campus recruiting trips. Manage travel plans. (10%) - Book and coordinate flights, rental cars, hotels, etc.; Drive rental vehicles when necessary; Help coordinate meals. Assist in administering team events. (5%) Assist and participate in athlete development programs (5%) - Freshmen Check-ins; Captain Meetings. The physical demands described here are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this position. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. Work is performed primarily in an office or campus setting , with occasional travel between buildings and to on- or off-campus meetings or events. Frequent sitting, talking, and hearing in meetings, classrooms, and office environments. Occasional walking, standing, bending, reaching, or lifting and carrying materials up to 25 pounds (such as files, books, and presentation equipment). Manual dexterity sufficient to operate a computer, telephone, and other standard office or instructional equipment. Visual acuity sufficient to read printed materials, digital screens, and documents. May involve extended periods of time at a computer workstation and participation in meetings conducted virtually or in person. May occasionally require attendance at evening or weekend events , such as student activities, faculty meetings, or institutional programs. Bachelor’s Degree Experience coaching optional level or higher NCAA experience preferred All applicants must provide: Cover letter outlining applicable experience and interest in the position Up-to-date resume Contact information for three professional referencest"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/190525": {
      "title": "Retention Coordinator, Student Support Services (SSS)/Advisor",
      "description": "Department: Simpson College Location: Indianola, IA Assist with planning, development, implementation, and delivery of all SSS programs and services. Assist students with individual needs, academic advisements, and counseling to project participants, including the Individual Educational Career Plan. Assist with progress reports and follow up on program participants. Serve on occasion as a liaison between SSS, college faculty, and community agencies. Coordination and training of peer mentors and supervision of the peer mentoring program. Coordination of the cultural activities for each program year. Serve on the campus Students of Concern Committee Master's degree required in Education, Counseling, or related academic area. Minimum 2 years of program experience in counseling or academic support services for low-income, first-generation, and/or minority students. Knowledge of collegiate academic and financial assistance procedures. Experience in networking and coordinating program activities. Preference given to candidates who have succeeded in overcoming barriers similar to those confronting the project’s target population Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Ideal start date is 08/31/2026 A complete application will include: 1) Cover letter addressing your interest in the position 2) Resume 3 ) Contact information of three professional references 4) Unofficial Graduate Transcripts"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/191755": {
      "title": "Part-time Campus Security Officer",
      "description": "Department: Simpson College: Student Development: Security Location: Indianola Summary To maintain a standard of safety and security for the campus, routinely patrol campus and parking lots, assist community members, and enforce the rules and regulations of Simpson College. This is a 12-month part-time ( generally two to three 8-hour shifts/week, including evening, nights & weekends) position. Essential Job Functions Secure campus buildings and provide regular foot and/or vehicle patrols of the entire campus, including checking doors, windows, life-safety devices, parking lots, etc. ( 40% ) Respond to calls for service, incidents, & emergencies promptly with a focus on customer service. ( 35% ) Maintain thorough and accurate duty logs. File incident reports as necessary. ( 5% ) Maintain communication with physical plant/custodial staff, housing staff, and co-workers. ( 5% ) Monitor surveillance cameras, alarms, and access points to buildings & campus . ( 5% ) Attending periodic training and meetings. ( 10% ) High school diploma or equivalent Knowledge of first aid and CPR (Simpson can provide training at no cost to you) Comfortable handling confidential information Experience using computer programs such as Word, Outlook, Teams, and Excel Previous work in security Interpersonal/communication skills: Position requires above-ordinary courtesy and tact to communicate effectively with diverse individuals in routine, high stress,and emergency situations. Also requires abilities to de-fuse emotionally charged situations and to write clearly Physical fitness: The ability to perform daily activities with endurance and strength, such as standing or walking around buildings, and lifting heavy items Problem-solving: The ability to find quick solutions to issues, react appropriately in stressful situations, and pay attention to details on rounds and when investigating Teamwork: The ability to work well in a team or alone and to be dependable Knowledge: Knowledge of standard security & safety protocols, legal guidelines, & relevant computer applications. Ability to type routine correspondence, forms, and use computer files/programs Physical Requirements: Ability to walk long distances for long periods of time; ability to move swiftly when needed. Some lifting is required . The physical demands described here are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this position. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. Work is performed primarily in an office or campus setting , with occasional travel between buildings and to on- or off-campus meetings or events. Frequent sitting, talking, and hearing in meetings, classrooms, and office environments. Occasional walking, standing, bending, reaching, or lifting and carrying materials up to 25 pounds (such as files, books, and presentation equipment). Manual dexterity sufficient to operate a computer, telephone, and other standard office or instructional equipment. Visual acuity sufficient to read printed materials, digital screens, and documents. May involve extended periods of time at a computer workstation and participation in meetings conducted virtually or in person. May occasionally require attendance at evening or weekend events , such as student activities, faculty meetings, or institutional programs. All applicants must submit: Cover Letter Resume 3 Professional References"
    }
